<task id="190" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Send budget inquiry sends Cc and Bcc end to end; the "Cc and Bcc are not sent" warning goes away on that step (D-222)</title>
    <phase>11 UAT (budget inquiry follow-up, D-222)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies .cs and .tsx code files.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Threads two optional fields through an existing path whose sink (CommunicationService.SendAsync) already sends and records Cc/Bcc; send-as-caller and ownership are unchanged.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>File overlap with task 191 (BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs, DecisionActionExecutors.cs): run 190 first, or rebase 191 onto it.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ontology</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>The Send budget inquiry step accepts Cc and Bcc but the server sends To only, and the step warns "Cc and Bcc are not sent with this step. Add every recipient to To." The owner chose to send them (D-222 (owner 2026-11-13, notes/decisions.md) (a); D-219 Q4).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core, the ontology decision route (IDecisionActionExecutor) and the DecisionWizard / EmailComposer.</role>
  <goal>For send-budget-inquiry only: optional `cc` and `bcc` catalog parameters, parsed and validated in Map like `to`, carried on BudgetInquiryRequest and set on SendCommunicationRequest.Cc/Bcc by InquiryEmailSender.Build; the wizard commits the composer's Cc/Bcc and shows no cc-not-sent warning for an action that declares them. send-reminder unchanged.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>DecisionActionCatalog.cs:160-165 MessageParameters (to/subject/body) is shared by send-budget-inquiry (:170-186) and send-reminder (:291-296). DecisionActionExecutors.cs:1537-1568 Map reads only `to` (split, de-dup, Address regex before any write). BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs:21-22 the request has no Cc/Bcc; Build :109-140 sets To only. The sink already sends Cc/Bcc and records sprk_cc/sprk_bcc and per-role participants (CommunicationService ~3181-3184, ~4916). ReadValues (DecisionCommitService.cs:1509-1516) refuses an undeclared parameter code, so cc/bcc must be catalog parameters. Client: EmailMessageFields.tsx:32 EMAIL_MESSAGE_CODES; :75-96 onStateChange commits to/subject/body only; :152-156 the warning (testid cc-not-sent). ParameterFields.tsx:306-313 shows the composer only when all three codes exist.</background>
    <relevant-files>
