  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change this task makes to Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md: no new endpoint, no new DI registration or package unless a criterion names it, and the publish-size delta against a fresh master build is measured and recorded in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every Dataverse write and the email send in this task stay AS THE CALLER (the inquiry email is sent by CommunicationService.SendAsync in SendMode.User, OBO); no app-only fallback is added on any path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Every refusal this task adds or changes on the decision route is a ProblemDetails with a stable reasonCode; never an unhandled 500.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests added in this task cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">D-222 (owner 2026-11-13, notes/decisions.md) (a): Cc and Bcc on the inquiry step are sent like the Send Email dialog and the warning goes away there.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: send-budget-inquiry only. Add cc/bcc to that action's parameters, NOT to the shared MessageParameters; send-reminder keeps its parameters, executor and warning.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse the shared EmailComposer (compose-only, EmailMessageFields); no new email form, endpoint, service or DI registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Map validates Cc and Bcc exactly as To (separators, de-dup, Address regex) before the preflight and before the service request is written.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012/021">Client changes stay in @spaarke/ui-components, no Xrm or auth import; no new UI element; light and dark unchanged.</constraint>
  </constraints>
