  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the line references on origin/master; record drift in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Catalog: optional `cc` and `bcc` Text parameters on send-budget-inquiry only.</step>
    <step order="3">BudgetInquiryRequest gains optional Cc/Bcc (default empty: existing calls compile unchanged). Map parses them; an address in To is not repeated in Cc/Bcc, one in Cc is not repeated in Bcc. Build sets Cc/Bcc (null when empty); the record-link choice stays keyed on To.</step>
    <step order="4">Client: EmailMessageFields commits cc/bcc (joined with "; ") and hides the warning when the action declares them; ParameterFields does not render cc/bcc as separate fields when the composer is shown; starting Cc/Bcc come from the step values.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per the acceptance criteria.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, the touched test classes and the Signals/Communication unit and data-mutation suites, plus jest on the DecisionWizard folder, tsc and ESLint on touched client files; all pass. Measure the BFF publish-size delta against a fresh master build (§10).</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations, the publish-size delta and the dev-check result in notes/task-190-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the review contract, plan read or client draft cannot carry two optional parameters without changing other actions, STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md §6); no side channel.</trigger>
    <trigger>If CommunicationService refuses or alters Cc/Bcc on an internal-only, archived, SendMode.User send, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>DecisionActionCatalog.cs:160-186 (no cc/bcc); BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs:21-22, :109-140 (To only); SendCommunicationRequest.Cc/Bcc already exist (Models/SendCommunicationRequest.cs:20,25).</existing>
    <extension>Yes, and this task IS the extension: two optional parameters on an existing action and two optional fields on an existing request.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A user who adds Cc or Bcc on the inquiry is told it will not be sent and must put everyone in To, so copied billing contacts get nothing or are exposed as direct recipients (owner UAT 2026-11-13).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Inquiry with Cc and Bcc">
      <steps>
        <step>On {org}, open a fee/scope budget Signal (fresh zz- communication) in the Console</step>
        <step>Take Send budget inquiry with To, Cc and Bcc; Record decision</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No cc-not-sent warning; recipients see To and Cc, the Bcc recipient gets it hidden; the sprk_communication row has sprk_cc and sprk_bcc; light and dark unchanged.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Reminder unchanged">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Do item, take Send a reminder, add a Cc</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The reminder step still shows its Cc warning.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
