  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given To, Cc and Bcc, the request Build returns has To, Cc and Bcc equal to the trimmed, de-duplicated addresses; associations, IsInternalOnly, ArchiveToSpe, CreateThreadPrivate, SendMode.User and body are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Cc or Bcc token that is not an email address, Map refuses with RecipientUnresolved naming the field, and no preflight, service-request create or send runs (assert the seams were not called).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given empty or absent cc and bcc, Cc and Bcc are null and the request equals today's To-only request; existing To-only tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An address in To and Cc (any case) is sent once, in To; one in Cc and Bcc is sent once, in Cc.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Bcc never appears in To, Cc, subject, body, footer or link lines (assert on the built request).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The send-budget-inquiry plan declares cc and bcc as optional; send-reminder's parameters are exactly as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Client: on the inquiry step a Cc is committed to the step's `cc` value and no cc-not-sent element renders; the existing F3b warning test is kept for a send-reminder action.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Client: Next stays disabled while any Cc or Bcc address is invalid, as for To.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched test classes and folders pass unchanged unless a criterion above names the change; BFF builds with no new warnings in touched files; tsc clean and no new ESLint errors in touched client files.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Owner UAT 2026-11-13 on MAT-34929-0040 (D-222 (owner 2026-11-13, notes/decisions.md)). Failed-send recovery is task 191. The composer already shows Cc/Bcc in compose-only mode; only the commit path and the warning change.</notes>
